TITLE: Angular Zoneless Change Detection Mechanisms
DESCRIPTION: In zoneless Angular applications, change detection relies on explicit notifications from core APIs rather than ZoneJS's monkey-patching. These mechanisms inform Angular when to run change detection and on which views, ensuring proper UI updates.
SOURCE: https://angular.dev/guide/zoneless

LANGUAGE: APIDOC
CODE:

```
Angular relies on notifications from core APIs to determine when to run change detection:
- ChangeDetectorRef.markForCheck (called automatically by AsyncPipe)
- ComponentRef.setInput
- Updating a signal that's read in a template
- Bound host or template listeners callbacks
- Attaching a view that was marked dirty by one of the above
```

