TITLE: Angular HTTP Interceptor: Add Authentication Header
DESCRIPTION: This TypeScript code demonstrates a common pattern in Angular HTTP interceptors: adding an authentication token to outgoing requests. It uses Angular's `inject` function to retrieve an `AuthService` instance, obtains the authentication token, and then clones the original `HttpRequest` to append the `X-Authentication-Token` header. The modified request is then passed to the next handler in the interceptor chain.
SOURCE: https://angular.dev/guide/http/interceptors

LANGUAGE: TypeScript
CODE:

```
const authToken = inject(AuthService).getAuthToken();

// Clone the request to add the authentication header.
const newReq = req.clone({
  headers: req.headers.append('X-Authentication-Token', authToken),
});
return next(newReq);
}
```

