TITLE: Configure Angular Testing Module for HTTP Mocking
DESCRIPTION: This snippet demonstrates how to set up the Angular testing module (`TestBed`) to enable HTTP client testing. It configures `ConfigService`, `provideHttpClient()`, and `provideHttpClientTesting()` to allow for mocking HTTP requests. It then shows how to inject `HttpTestingController` and a `ConfigService` to initiate an HTTP request for configuration data, preparing for a mock response.
